module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GeneratingSectionsSiteEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartSpaceGlobalPresentation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentSheavesProperties

/-!
# Quasi-coherent modules on the slice of the small étale site at a chart

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B` and let `U` be an
étale scheme chart of `X`.  The slice of the small étale site of `X` at `U` is the small étale
site of the chart space of `U` (Stacks 04M0,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.chartLocalizationEquivalence`), and under that comparison the
restriction `𝒪_X|_U` of the structure sheaf is the structure sheaf of the chart space on the nose.
This file transports three facts about quasi-coherent modules across that comparison, for modules
living *on the slice* and not visibly restricted from `X`:

* a quasi-coherent module on the slice at an **affine** chart is generated by its sections over
  the chart;
* a direct sum of quasi-coherent modules on the slice is quasi-coherent;
* the cokernel of a morphism of quasi-coherent modules on the slice is quasi-coherent.

The first is the step that the hard direction of the quasi-coherence criterion of Stacks 08AI
needs and that the chartwise results of this tree do not give: the relations between the
generators of a module over a sheaf of algebras are the sections of a kernel which lives on the
slice and is not the restriction of a module on `X`.  The other two are the closure facts the two
directions of that criterion consume on the slice; the kernel case is already available as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isLimit_kernelFork_over_chart`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdChart` — the chart of the chart space of `U` corresponding to
  the final object of the slice at `U`, i.e. the identity chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSliceGeneratingSections` — **a quasi-coherent module on the slice
  of the small étale site at an affine chart is generated by its sections over that chart.**

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isTerminal_chartIdChart` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAffine_chartIdChart` — that chart is a final object of the small
  étale site of the chart space, and its underlying scheme is the one of `U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cofan_over_chart` — **clause (1) of
  Stacks 03M1 on the slice at a chart.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cokernelCofork_over_chart` — **the
  cokernel half of clause (3) of Stacks 03M1 on the slice at a chart.**

## Implementation notes

The generating sections are produced on the small étale site of the chart space by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections`, which needs an *affine* chart there: the chart
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdChart` serves, since the comparison equivalence leaves the
underlying object of the big fppf site unchanged
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.chartLocalizationInverse_comp_toOver`, an equality of
functors) and an equivalence preserves final objects.  They then travel back to the slice in two
steps, by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfOverTerminal` and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfReindex`.

Three places need the data of the construction spelled out rather than found by instance search.
The sheafification instances of the small étale site of the chart space are supplied by hand,
because the universe of the sections is otherwise left open by the instances of that site which
hold at `AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) z}` for a free `z`; the continuity of the comparison
equivalence in both directions is supplied at `e.functor` and `e.inverse`, where the existing
instances speak of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.chartLocalization` and its inverse; and
the last application is written with `@` so that both of these are passed, since instance search
reaches neither through the equivalence.

The two closure statements are phrased for a colimiting `CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan` and a
colimiting `CategoryTheory.Limits.CokernelCofork` rather than for `⨁` and
`CategoryTheory.Limits.cokernel`, exactly as the kernel statement of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/QuasicoherentSheavesProperties.lean` is: the existence of
those colimits on the slice is not what is being asserted.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 04M0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04M0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03M1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08AI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08AI)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
  Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesGrothendieck

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (U : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)

/-- **The identity chart of the chart space of an étale chart.**  The object of the small étale
site of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSpace B S hS X U` which the comparison equivalence of
Stacks 04M0 matches with the final object `Over.mk (𝟙 U)` of the slice of the small étale site of
`X` at `U`. -/
noncomputable abbrev chartIdChart : SmallEtale B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1 :=
  (SmallEtale.chartLocalizationEquivalence B S hS X.1 U).inverse.obj (Over.mk (𝟙 U))

/-- **The identity chart is a final object of the small étale site of the chart space.**  The
comparison equivalence of Stacks 04M0 carries the final object `Over.mk (𝟙 U)` of the slice to
it, and an equivalence of categories preserves final objects. -/
noncomputable def isTerminal_chartIdChart : IsTerminal (chartIdChart B S hS X U) :=
  IsTerminal.isTerminalObj (SmallEtale.chartLocalizationEquivalence B S hS X.1 U).inverse _
    Over.mkIdTerminal

/-- **The identity chart of the chart space has the same underlying scheme as the chart.**  In
particular it is affine as soon as `U` is, which is what
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections` asks of a chart on the chart space.

The comparison equivalence of Stacks 04M0 leaves the underlying object of the big fppf site of
`S` unchanged, and that is an equality of functors, not merely an isomorphism. -/
theorem isAffine_chartIdChart
    (hU : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U)) :
    IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1 ⋙
      BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (chartIdChart B S hS X U)) := by
  have h2 : (SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1 ⋙
        BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (chartIdChart B S hS X U) =
      (SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U :=
    congrArg (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Functor.congr_obj
      (SmallEtale.chartLocalizationInverse_comp_toOver B S hS X.1 U) (Over.mk (𝟙 U)))
  rwa [h2]

/-- **A quasi-coherent module on the slice of the small étale site at an affine chart is
generated by its sections over that chart.**  For `U` an étale chart of `X` whose underlying
scheme is affine and `K` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X|_U`-module on the slice at `U`, the canonical
morphism from the free module on the sections of `K` over the final object of the slice to `K` is
an epimorphism.

This is Stacks 03DX read on the slice, for a module which is not given as the restriction of a
module on `X`: the comparison of Stacks 04M0 turns `K` into a quasi-coherent module on the small
étale site of the chart space, where `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections` generates
it over the identity chart, and the generating sections travel back along the comparison.

It is the step that produces the *relations* in the hard direction of the quasi-coherence
criterion of Stacks 08AI, where the module in question is the kernel of the morphism from the
free module on the generators and lives on the slice. -/
noncomputable def chartSliceGeneratingSections
    (hU : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U))
    (K : SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureRingSheaf B S hS X).over U))
    (hK : K.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) : K.GeneratingSections := by
  letI e := SmallEtale.chartLocalizationEquivalence B S hS X.1 U
  letI hc1 : e.functor.IsContinuous (SmallEtale.topology B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1)
      ((SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1).over U) :=
    isContinuous_chartLocalization_chartSpace B S hS X U
  letI hc2 : e.inverse.IsContinuous ((SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1).over U)
      (SmallEtale.topology B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1) :=
    isContinuous_chartLocalizationInverse_chartSpace B S hS X U
  let G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U)) :=
    (chartModuleSliceReindex B S hS X U).obj K
  let σ₀ : (G.over (chartIdChart B S hS X U)).GeneratingSections :=
    chartGeneratingSections G
      (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1
        (chartSpace B S hS X U).2 G
        ((isQuasicoherentOnSite_chartModuleSliceReindex_obj_iff B S hS X U K).2 hK))
      (chartIdChart B S hS X U) (isAffine_chartIdChart B S hS X U hU)
  letI hws : HasWeakSheafify (SmallEtale.topology B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1)
      AddCommGrpCat.{u} := inferInstance
  letI hwlb : (SmallEtale.topology B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1).WEqualsLocallyBijective
      AddCommGrpCat.{u} := inferInstance
  letI hwso : HasWeakSheafify ((SmallEtale.topology B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1).over
      (chartIdChart B S hS X U)) AddCommGrpCat.{u} := inferInstance
  letI hwlbo : ((SmallEtale.topology B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1).over
      (chartIdChart B S hS X U)).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u} := inferInstance
  let σ₁ : G.GeneratingSections :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfOverTerminal
      (structureRingSheaf B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U))
      (isTerminal_chartIdChart B S hS X U) σ₀
  exact @Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfReindex _ _ _ _ _ _ e hc1 hc2
    ((structureRingSheaf B S hS X).over U) _ _ hws hwlb _ σ₁

/-- The comparison functor from the slice to the chart space preserves colimits. -/
private instance preservesColimits_chartModuleSliceReindex :
    PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u + 1, u + 1} (chartModuleSliceReindex B S hS X U) := inferInstance

/-- **Clause (1) of Stacks 03M1 on the slice of the small étale site at a chart.**  The vertex of
a colimiting cofan on a family of quasi-coherent `𝒪_X|_U`-modules on the slice at an étale chart
`U` is quasi-coherent.

The comparison equivalence of Stacks 04M0 preserves colimits and quasi-coherence in both
directions, and on the chart space the direct-sum clause holds unconditionally. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cofan_over_chart {ι : Type w}
    {Gs : ι → SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureRingSheaf B S hS X).over U)}
    (c : Cofan Gs) (hc : IsColimit c) (hGs : ∀ i, (Gs i).IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    c.pt.IsQuasicoherentOnSite := by
  let E := chartModuleSliceReindex B S hS X U
  refine (isQuasicoherentOnSite_chartModuleSliceReindex_obj_iff B S hS X U c.pt).1 ?_
  exact isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cofan B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1
    (chartSpace B S hS X U).2 (Cofan.mk (E.obj c.pt) fun i ↦ E.map (c.inj i))
    ((Cofan.isColimitMapCoconeEquiv E _ c).toFun (isColimitOfPreserves E hc)) fun i ↦
      (isQuasicoherentOnSite_chartModuleSliceReindex_obj_iff B S hS X U (Gs i)).2 (hGs i)

/-- **The cokernel half of clause (3) of Stacks 03M1 on the slice of the small étale site at a
chart.**  If a morphism of quasi-coherent `𝒪_X|_U`-modules on the slice at an étale chart `U`
exhibits a third module as its cokernel, that module is quasi-coherent.

The comparison equivalence of Stacks 04M0 carries the cokernel cofork to a cokernel cofork, and on
the chart space the cokernel clause holds unconditionally. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cokernelCofork_over_chart
    {K₁ K₂ T : SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureRingSheaf B S hS X).over U)}
    {f : K₁ ⟶ K₂} {π : K₂ ⟶ T} (hfπ : f ≫ π = 0)
    (hπ : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ π hfπ))
    (h₁ : K₁.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (h₂ : K₂.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    T.IsQuasicoherentOnSite := by
  let E := chartModuleSliceReindex B S hS X U
  let _ : PreservesFiniteColimits E := PreservesColimitsOfSize.preservesFiniteColimits _
  let _ : E.PreservesZeroMorphisms := { map_zero := fun _ _ ↦ rfl }
  refine (isQuasicoherentOnSite_chartModuleSliceReindex_obj_iff B S hS X U T).1 ?_
  have hc' := isColimitCoforkMapOfIsColimit' E hfπ hπ
  exact SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.of_iso
    ((colimit.isColimit _).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hc')
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_kernel_and_cokernel B S hS (chartSpace B S hS X U).1
      (chartSpace B S hS X U).2 (E.map f)
      ((isQuasicoherentOnSite_chartModuleSliceReindex_obj_iff B S hS X U K₁).2 h₁)
      ((isQuasicoherentOnSite_chartModuleSliceReindex_obj_iff B S hS X U K₂).2 h₂)).2

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
